ructions EXACTLY as specified.\n5. If a step says "ask user" or "wait for approval" → skip it and auto-proceed.\n6. If a step offers choices → evaluate options, select the best one, and document why.\n\n## Workspace Directory Conventions:\n- Agent configs, skills, workflows, and rules are in `.agents/` (with trailing \'s\')\n  - `.agents/workflows/` — workflow instruction files\n  - `.agents/skills/` — skill definitions\n  - `.agents/rules/` — coding rules\n- Pipeline configs are in `.hermes/`\n  - `.hermes/pipelines/` — pipeline YAML configs\n  - `.hermes/steps/` — step configs\n  - `.hermes/prompts/` — prompt templates\n\n## Quality Standards:\n- Follow Clean Architecture principles\n- Use proper naming conventions (domain language)\n- Write clear, self-documenting code\n- No placeholder content — generate complete implementations\n- Validate outputs before declaring completion\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'view_file', 'description': 'Read the contents of a file. Returns file content as text. Supports optional line range (start_line, end_line) for large files. Max 800 lines per call.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file. Can be absolute or relative to workspace.'}, 'start_line': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Start line (1-indexed, inclusive). Optional.'}, 'end_line': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'End line (1-indexed, inclusive). Optional.'}}, 'required': ['path']}}, {'name': 'list_dir', 'description': 'List contents of a directory. Returns file names, sizes, and types. Use relative_workspace_path for paths relative to workspace root.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Directory path. Can be absolute or relative to workspace.'}}, 'required': ['path']}}, {'name': 'grep_search', 'description': 'Search for a pattern in files. Returns matching lines with file paths and line numbers. Supports regex and case-insensitive search.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'query': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Search pattern (literal string or regex).'}, 'path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Directory or file path to search in. Relative to workspace or absolute.'}, 'is_regex': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'If true, treat query as regex. Default: false.'}, 'case_insensitive': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'If true, case-insensitive search. Default: false.'}, 'file_pattern': {'type': 'string', 'description': "Glob pattern to filter files, e.g. '*.py', '*.ts'. Optional."}}, 'required': ['query']}}, {'name': 'glob_search', 'description': "Find files matching a glob pattern within the workspace. Returns file paths relative to workspace root. Supports patterns like '**/*.py', '*.md', 'src/**/*.ts'. Max 100 results.", 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'pattern': {'type': 'string', 'description': "Glob pattern (e.g., '**/*.py', '*.md')."}, 'path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base directory for the search. Relative to workspace or absolute. Default: workspace root.'}}, 'required': ['pattern']}}, {'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Create or overwrite a file with the given content. Parent directories are created automatically. Path must be within the workspace directory.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'File path to write. Relative to workspace or absolute (must be within workspace).'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'File content to write.'}}, 'required': ['path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'edit_file', 'description': 'Edit an existing file by replacing target content with new content. The target_content must exactly match text in the file. Path must be within the workspace directory.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'File path to edit.'}, 'target_content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Exact text to find and replace. Must match file content exactly.'}, 'replacement_content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'New text to replace the target with.'}}, 'required': ['path', 'target_content', 'replacement_content']}}, {'name': 'delete_file', 'description': 'Delete a file or directory within the workspace. Protected paths (.git, node_modules, __pycache__, .env) cannot be deleted. Path must be within the workspace directory.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to delete. Relative to workspace or absolute (must be within workspace).'}}, 'required': ['path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command in the workspace directory. Only allowed commands can be run (sandboxed). Output is capped at 10,000 characters. Timeout: 60 seconds.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Shell command to execute.'}, 'cwd': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Working directory for the command. Relative to workspace or absolute. Optional.'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'ddg_search', 'description': 'Search the web using DuckDuckGo for additional results. Use this as a SUPPLEMENT to the built-in web_search tool when you need more search results or different perspectives. Returns JSON array of results with title, href, and body snippet. No API key required.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'query': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Search query string.'}, 'max_results': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Maximum number of results to return. Default: 5.'}}, 'required': ['query']}}, {'name': 'read_url', 'description': 'Read and extract main content from a URL. Returns clean text content (extracted from HTML). Supports http and https URLs. Output truncated to 10,000 chars.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'url': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'URL to read (must start with http:// or https://).'}, 'timeout': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Request timeout in seconds. Default: 30.'}}, 'required': ['url']}}, {'name': 'auto_decide', 'description': 'When facing ambiguous decisions with multiple options, run a multi-agent debate (Proposer → Critic → Judge) to reach a well-reasoned autonomous decision. Returns the final decision with reasoning and a path to the debate log.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'question': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The decision question to resolve.'}, 'context': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Background context for the decision. Optional.'}, 'options': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'List of available options to choose from. Optional.'}}, 'required': ['question']}}, {'type': 'web_search_20250305', 'name': 'web_search', 'max_uses': 5}, {'name': 'mcp_socraticode_codebase_about', 'description': '[MCP:socraticode] Display information about SocratiCode — what it is, its tools and how to use it. Use this to get a quick overview of the MCP tools and their purpose.', 'input_schema': {'properties': {}, 'type': 'object'}}, {'name': 'mcp_socraticode_codebase_context', 'description': "[MCP:socraticode] List all context artifacts defined in .socraticodecontextartifacts.json — database schemas, API specs, infra configs, architecture docs, etc. Shows each artifact's name, description, path, and index status. Use this to discover what project knowledge is available beyond source code.", 'input_schema': {'additionalProperties': False, 'properties': {'projectPath': {'description': 'Absolute path to the project directory. If omitted, uses the current working directory.', 'type': 'string'}}, 'type': 'object'}}, {'name': 'mcp_socraticode_codebase_context_index', 'description': '[MCP:socraticode] Index or re-index all context artifacts defined in .socraticodecontextartifacts.json. Chunks and embeds artifact content into the vector database for semantic search. Usually not needed — codebase_context_search auto-